Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Spore-Pods Smother the Repeater
- Story & Context: Deep-sea technician Angus Ross was inspecting a fractured optical junction box four hundred meters down on the Wyville Thomson Ridge when his helmet hydrophone picked up a rhythmic shudder—not an electrical ground fault, but sea-lichen and tube-worms vibrating the casing like a reed—which caused his breathing gas regulator to rattle violently in his teeth. Back in the repair vessel’s galley, while copper-tasting salt water still crusted in his ears, he plugged Vance’s tenor sax straight into an overdriven telemetry channel and laid down the backing track while storm waves battered the hull. The take captures the terrifying calm of deep water before industrial machinery kicks in, immortalized by Vance’s whispered opening cry: "Down where the glass threads bleed, the iron learns to breathe."
