Track 2: Brighid's Glasshouse at Rockall
- Story & Context: In a storm-battered geodesic greenhouse on the cliffs of North Uist, botanist and keyboardist Brighid Campbell suffered an emotional collapse after losing her research grant, locking herself inside with a portable four-track recorder and an overdriven baritone amplifier while the smell of damp peat and scorched vacuum tubes choked the humid air. When local harbor officials pounded on the glass demanding she turn off the shuddering bass tones that were cracking the nursery panes, she responded by feeding Vance's live sax takes through a ring modulator at deafening volume. Collapsing among shattered glass and trampled fern fronds, she left her raw vocal track unedited on the master tape, sobbing the confession: "I buried your letters under seven miles of brine and copper wire."
