Track 3: "Is That Daylight or Fiber-Leak?"
- Story & Context: Following the mysterious decommissioning of the Rockall data station, local trawler captain Donald Macleod pulled up a net snarled in glowing fiber-optic strands that pulsed with an unexplainable acoustic resonance, filling the wheelhouse with the scent of ozone and rotting kelp. The crew listened in awe as the boat’s sonar screen glitched into drifting botanical shapes, their speakers broadcasting an eerie, ambient hum that sounded like a brass section playing through six miles of seawater. The song preserves that unearthly salvage recording layered under crashing drop-tuned industrial guitars, concluding with the legendary radio transmission that became scene gospel: "The current broke our bodies, but it kept the orchard lit."
